>Teleportitis is gained by eating a leprechaun or quantum mechanic or nymph.

No... this is 2.3 info.  Nowadays, teleportitis is caused randomly, not
always, by eating anything that teleports.  Leprechauns and nymphs
are examples; quantum mechanics are NOT - eating a quantum mechanic will
toggle your speed.  Tengus are a _very_ good thing to eat - normally
give you teleportitis, but once in a while they will give you intrinsic
teleport control.

>It is NOT a curse (IMHO).  After a while, you'll gain control and be able to
>teleport at will (a truly amazing escape power)....

Agreed.  However, when you don't have control of yourself, it can be
a nuisance.

